**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 §H and §S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. Writing an item first snapshots and pins the model version it references (001 §I 'the ItemModel it instantiates (pinned and snapshotted)'; 001 §E 'Library closure snapshot'; 001 §C 'A version becomes Pinned … when a kit first references it'; the S7.1 brief: referencing a model version snapshots and pins it (S4.2); step 139: S7.1's items call `snapshotReferences`). In `KitContentFiles.fs`, on step 149's `type KitLibraryContext with` extension, documented in one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.1: `member this.recordItem (item : Item) : Result<unit, KitLibraryError>` calls `this.snapshotReferences item.libraryReferences` (steps 139, 215), then `this.kit.proxy.writeItem item` (step 218), a `KitError` wrapped as `KitLibraryKitErr`. The snapshots come first, so a written item never references a version the kit lacks; on a failure the file is not written and what the snapshot wrote stays (step 139). The Items panel (S7.2) and Publish calibration (S11.5) record items through it. No other member is added. Tests, new facts in `KitLibraryTests` (step 139), over its Built-in library (`BuiltinCatalogue.freshStores ()`, which holds the shipped item models since step 210), its recorder of pins and its in-memory kit opened read-write. `recording an item snapshots its model's library version and pins it, then writes its file`: CPL1 made through `ItemDraft.toItem` over `LibraryModelChoice (BuiltinCatalogue.itemModel ItemModelIds.circularPolarizerModelId)`, recorded through `recordItem`, leaves `listSnapshots` holding exactly that item model's version 1 envelope, `paths` holding `library/<its GUID>@v1.item-model-json` and `CPL1.item-json`, the recorder holding that version, and `kit.proxy.readItems ()` answering CPL1. `recording a sample item snapshots the sample with its materials and their categories`: a QZ item over `StackSampleChoice` of `SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId` at version 1 snapshots the sample, its glass material and that material's category, each once. `recording a preset item snapshots the preset's latest version`: a laser item over `SourcePresetChoice` of `PresetIds.heNe633` snapshots that preset's version 1. `a read-only kit records no item`: over a context opened with `ReadOnlyKitAccess`, `recordItem` answers `KitLibraryKitErr (KitReadOnlyErr _)`, the recorder is empty and `paths` is unchanged. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved. The item file/schema and snapshot tests MUST cover source, ideal-polarizer and stack items carrying their exact ItemModel version and typed physics binding. recordItem MUST pin and snapshot the model and the full physics closure. Reopening against an empty library MUST resolve the model from its .item-model-json snapshot and then its binding; a missing model MUST be a typed error, never a preset/sample fallback. No fixture MAY construct a bare preset/sample model instance.

**Acceptance.** After recording lands, `KitLibraryContext.recordItem` MUST snapshot and pin the library version an item's model names, with its closure, before it writes the item's file, and write nothing under a read-only kit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `recording an item snapshots its model's library version and pins it, then writes its file`, `recording a sample item snapshots the sample with its materials and their categories`, `recording a preset item snapshots the preset's latest version` and `a read-only kit records no item`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.
